{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/dataformatting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"title":"Data formatting"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DataFormatting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Data-formatting","title":"Data formatting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle"]},{"anchor":"Data-parsing","title":"Data parsing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Convert numbers, dates, measurements, and other values to and from locale-aware string representations.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Fundamentals","title":"Fundamentals","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/NumbersDataAndBasicValues","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/StringsAndText","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Collections","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DatesAndTimes","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FiltersAndSorting"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FoundationEssentials defines the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol to establish conventions for formatting a given type as some kind of output type, typically a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Similarly, the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol provides an API for converting a representation back to the represented type, such as converting a numeric string to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While FoundationEssentials defines the core protocols, most implementations of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" exist in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":" module."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":" also extends types in both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationEssentials"},{"type":"text","text":" and the Swift Standard Library to add formatting and parsing support."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you import "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":", you have two general approaches to perform formatting of supported types:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted()"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the type, optionally passing in a customized "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" appropriate to the type. These methods, defined by extensions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":", are useful for performing one-off formatting with default styles or slightly-customized styles."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", passing in the type you want to format. This method, defined by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" itself, makes sense when you customize a style and want to format many instances with it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrangement is similar with parsing:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:format:lenient:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to create instance of a type from its formatted representation. For example, to create a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" from the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":", you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var oneTwoThree = try Double(\"1.23\", format: FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>())"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" to initialize an instance of the output type. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var fourFiveSix = try FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().parseStrategy.parse(\"4.56\")"},{"type":"text","text":" creates a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" equal to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4.56"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"references":{"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Decimal":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A structure representing a base-10 number."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Decimal"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Decimal"}],"title":"Decimal","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/decimal","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/ParseableFormatStyle":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ParseableFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ParseableFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ParseableFormatStyle","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/parseableformatstyle","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that can convert a given input data type into a representation in an output type."}]},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials","title":"FoundationEssentials","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Access essential data types, collections, and operating-system services to define the base layer of functionality for your app."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/DiscreteFormatStyle":{"abstract":[{"text":"A format style that transforms a continuous input into a discrete output and provides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information about its discretization boundaries.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscreteFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/discreteformatstyle","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiscreteFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","title":"DiscreteFormatStyle"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/NumbersDataAndBasicValues":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/NumbersDataAndBasicValues","title":"Numbers, data, and basic values","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/numbersdataandbasicvalues","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Work with primitive values and other fundamental types."}]},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Collections":{"url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/collections","title":"Collections","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Collections","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use specialized collections to store and iterate groups of objects or values."}],"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/FormatStyle":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"FormatStyle","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/formatstyle","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that converts a given data type into a representation in another type, such as a string."}]},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/DatesAndTimes":{"url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/datesandtimes","title":"Dates and times","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DatesAndTimes","kind":"article","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/StringsAndText":{"abstract":[],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Strings and text","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/StringsAndText","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/stringsandtext"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/ParseStrategy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that parses an input representation, such as a formatted string, into a provided data type."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ParseStrategy"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ParseStrategy","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ParseStrategy"}],"url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/parsestrategy"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/FiltersAndSorting":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FiltersAndSorting","title":"Filters and sorting","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/filtersandsorting","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[]}}}